  "latestNews": {
    "slug": "dread-eleven-tactical-camp-ahead-of-divisional-championship",
    "title": "Dread Eleven Convenes High-Velocity Tactical Camp at Martand Ground",
    "summary": "Skipper Akhil Mishra convenes a 43-man tactical camp at Martand Ground ahead of the Atal Bihari Vajpayee Memorial Tournament circuit.",
    "publishedAt": "2024-11-10T10:00:00Z",
    "updatedAt": "2024-11-10T14:00:00Z",
    "author": {
      "name": "DE Tactical Cell",
      "role": "Chief Analyst"
    },
    "heroImage": "/public/de-hero.jpg",
    "category": "Tactical Dossier",
    "readTime": "4 min read",
    "body": "<p>Rewa — Dread Eleven (DE) have commenced their intensive tactical drills at Martand Ground No. 3, confirming a 43-man roster spearheaded by veteran captain <strong>Akhil Mishra</strong>.</p>\n<p>Coming off 13 verified tournament victories across 24 fixtures, Dread Eleven are sharpening their death-overs execution and powerplay containment.</p>\n<p>\"Our track record in Rewa speaks for itself,\" Mishra noted. \"With Kuldeep Sen operating at peak velocity, Kumar Kartikeya controlling the middle overs, and Ashwin Das executing at the death, Dread Eleven possess the most balanced bowling attack in the division.\"</p>\n<p>The coaching staff introduced comprehensive video analytics focusing on boundary prevention inside the 30-yard ring. Field positioning strategies were rigorously simulated under synthetic floodlights to replicate pressure situations during tournament knockout clashes.</p>\n<p>Furthermore, middle-order partnerships were tested against dual-spin tandems, reinforcing situational batting templates. The squad will conclude the 10-day preparatory camp with three intra-squad practice matches at APSU Stadium before the opening derby fixture.</p>\n"
